From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 22:24:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH v2] mac80211: let a driver mirror the mesh path table

A device that forwards 802.11s frames itself needs the mesh path and
proxy tables, and it sees path use and proxied addresses that the stack
does not.

Add config_mesh_offload_path(), called in atomic context whenever a path
or proxy is added, changed, deactivated or deleted, and
ieee80211_mesh_path_offld_change_notify() for the device to report a path
in use, a destination it has no path to, an expired path, or a proxy it
learned. The mesh TTL, path refresh time and forwarding setting are copied
into the BSS configuration when the mesh starts and when they change.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5

Rebase this NSS integration onto the shared mac80211/ath11k patch
series while preserving the local host-path fixes.

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
---
